              "fig-choice-n37-cubic-B"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "C",
            "text": "$y=x^3$ is increasing on $\\mathbb R$; $y=-x^3$ is decreasing on $\\mathbb R$. Neither has an interval with the opposite direction.",
            "figure_ids": [
              "fig-choice-n37-cubic-C"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "D",
            "text": "$y=x^3$ decreases on $(-\\infty,0]$ and increases on $[0,\\infty)$; $y=-x^3$ increases on $(-\\infty,0]$ and decreases on $[0,\\infty)$.",
