      "intent": {
        "task": "Recognize both cubic sketches and their global monotonicity.",
        "source_solution": "Task: sketch two functions and state increasing/decreasing input sets.\na: x^3 passes through (-1,-1),(0,0),(1,1), is odd and strictly increasing\non R. For u<v, v^3-u^3=(v-u)(v^2+uv+u^2)>0; the second factor cannot\nbe zero for distinct u,v. No decreasing interval exists.\nb: -x^3 passes through (-1,1),(0,0),(1,-1); reflecting across the x-axis\nmakes it strictly decreasing on R. No increasing interval exists.\nAn isolated horizontal tangent at 0 does not split strict monotonicity.\nLoss: recognizing both finished sketches is not independent drawing.",
        "unit_reason": "One complete two-function study includes both sketches and input sets. The two reflected functions are kept together to avoid a separately displayed answer supplying the reflection.",
        "concept_blocks": [],
        "limitations": [
          "Recognition of finished sketches does not demonstrate independently drawing either cubic.",
          "Only a finite window is drawn; whole-real-line monotonicity still requires reasoning from the formulas."
        ],
        "figure_observations": [
