            "observation": "Opened complete 640x420 PNG once. Left heading y=x^3 has a descending S curve; right heading y=-x^3 has an ascending S curve. Both flatten at the origin. +/-1.5 x ticks, +/-3 y ticks, both axis arrows and both bottom origin captions are visible. This records the declared sign-exchanged alternative, not an approval."
          },
          {
            "figure_id": "fig-choice-n37-cubic-B",
            "observation": "Opened complete 640x420 PNG once. Left cubic rises from bottom-left through the origin to top-right; right cubic descends with the reflected shape. Both have visibly flat central tangents. Both right edges, lower endpoints, +/-1.5 and +/-3 ticks and origin captions are visible. Independent review remains pending."
          },
          {
            "figure_id": "fig-choice-n37-cubic-C",
            "observation": "Opened complete 640x420 PNG once. Under the two cubic headings, the curves are deliberately straight rising and falling lines, with nonhorizontal central slopes and smaller endpoint heights than the cubics. Axes, all tick labels and both origin captions are fully visible."
          },
          {
            "figure_id": "fig-choice-n37-cubic-D",
            "observation": "Opened complete 640x420 PNG once. Under cubic headings, the left graph is a U and the right an inverted U, both turning at zero and having equal heights at opposite inputs. They are the declared even-power distractors. The full right panel and both bottom captions are visible."
          }
