      "intent": {
        "task": "Recognize complete numerical and parameterized quadratic studies.",
        "source_solution": "Task: sketch four quadratic functions and specify monotonic intervals.\na: 1.73x^2 is upward, vertex (0,0), passes through (+/-1,1.73);\ndecreases on (-infinity,0], increases on [0,infinity).\nb: -14.8x^2 is downward, vertex (0,0), passes through (+/-1,-14.8);\nincreases on (-infinity,0], decreases on [0,infinity).\nc: ax^2, a>0, has the same orientation and monotonicity as a; points\n(+/-1,a), vertex minimum 0. The height is parameter dependent.\nd: ax^2, a<0, has the same orientation and monotonicity as b; points\n(+/-1,a), vertex maximum 0. The height is parameter dependent.\nFor two nonnegative inputs, x^2 increases; for two nonpositive inputs it\ndecreases. Multiplying by a negative coefficient reverses comparisons.\nIncluding the common endpoint 0 in both maximal half-line domains is valid:\nstrict monotonicity compares distinct inputs, and 0 is the turning point.\nOther endpoint conventions must not be offered as false alternatives.\nGeneral graphs use vertical axis y/|a| for a normalized sketch, visibly labelled;\nnumeric graphs keep actual y with signed value markings. No fixed a is invented.\nLoss: recognizing sketches and intervals is not producing them.",
        "unit_reason": "A native multiple response selects all valid two-function studies, preserving all four original graphs without repeating the same sign rule in separately revealing questions.",
        "concept_blocks": [],
        "limitations": [
