    {
      "id": "q31",
      "source_numbers": [
        "798"
      ],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "For every real $x>5$, let $E=\\left(\\frac{x+5}{x^2-5x}-\\frac{x}{x^2-25}\\right)\\frac{x^2-25}{5}$. Which argument proves $2<E<3$ for every such $x$?",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "A",
            "text": "After factoring, $E=2+5/x$. Since $x>5$, $5/x>1$, so $E>3$.",
            "figure_ids": []
          },
          {
            "id": "B",
            "text": "For $x=10$, $E=2.5$ and $2<2.5<3$. This proves the bound for every $x>5$.",
            "figure_ids": []
          },
          {
            "id": "C",
            "text": "Factoring gives $E=2+5/x$. Since $x>5$, $5/x>0$, so $E>2$. This establishes both requested bounds.",
            "figure_ids": []
          },
          {
            "id": "D",
            "text": "The denominators are nonzero. Factoring gives $E=(x+5)^2/(5x)-x/5=2+5/x$. Since $x>5$, $0<5/x<1$, hence $2<E<3$.",
            "figure_ids": []
          }
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Prove the universal strict bound through legal simplification.",
        "source_solution": "Task: prove the expression lies strictly between 2 and 3 for every x>5.\nLet E=((x+5)/(x^2-5x)-x/(x^2-25))*(x^2-25)/5.\nSince x>5, x, x-5 and x+5 are nonzero; factor the denominators.\nE=(x+5)^2/(5x)-x/5=(10x+25)/(5x)=2+5/x.\nFor x>5, 0<5/x<1, so 2<E<3. Bounds 2 and 3 are not attained.\nDistinction: legal denominator cancellation and a strict reciprocal bound;\na single numerical example is not a universal proof.",
        "unit_reason": "A complete algebraic argument must establish the claimed interval for every permitted input, not one numerical instance.",
        "concept_blocks": [],
        "limitations": [
          "Recognizing a universal proof does not demonstrate independently composing the algebra or reciprocal inequalities."
        ],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": [
          "D"
        ],
        "rationales": [
          {
